## union.rs.vm
## Generates a Rust enum (data-carrying) for an IDL union declaration.
##
## Unlike the C# mapping (a sealed class with a discriminant property and
## per-branch typed accessors — C# has no idiomatic discriminated-union type;
## see docs/csharp-binding-guide.md §14), Rust's own `enum` *is* a tagged
## union, so this is a direct, idiomatic mapping rather than a workaround.
## The IDL discriminant value itself is not preserved as data: Rust manages
## the enum's tag internally, so match on the variant instead of comparing
## against the original switch value.
##
## Not derived: Default. Rust's #[default] attribute is only legal on a
## unit variant (rustc: "the #[default] attribute may only be used on unit
## enum variants"), and every union case here carries a payload -- so, unlike
## enum.rs.vm's plain C-like enum, no case can ever be marked #[default].
## This is also why struct.rs.vm does not derive Default: a struct embedding
## one of these unions as a field would fail to derive it transitively.
##
## Context:
##   $union — UnionNode
##   $types — TypeResolver
##
#![allow(non_snake_case, non_camel_case_types)]
##
/// Rust enum for IDL union `${union.name}`.
/// IDL discriminant type: `#rustType($union.switchType)` (not preserved as
/// data — match on the variant instead of the original switch value).
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
pub enum $types.safeName($union.name) {
#foreach($case in $union.cases)
    /// #if($case.default)Default case.#{else}IDL label(s): $case.labels#end
    $types.toPascalCase($case.name)(#rustType($case.type)),
#end
}
